kings":[]},"task_tags":["digital_watermarking"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/access.2020.3006980","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/access.2020.3006980","citation_count":7,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/access.2020.3006980","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/access.2020.3006980","query":"image watermarking @ IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:43:11Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-e4684a2957c21bbb","title":"Steganalysis by Recombining Spatial Rich Model","title_zh":"","year":2019,"publication_date":"2019-12-01","abstract":"Abstract Steganalysis is an important topic in the field of information security. Steganalysis is mainly based on the traditional machine learning method, represented by the spatial rich model, and has high detection performance. Aiming at the problems of high feature dimension, strong redundancy and long feature extraction time in the spatial rich model, this paper conducts a series of feature selection operations and explores four different model combination methods: single quantization factor combination method, single filter kernel type combination method, mixed selecting combination method, Pearson correlation coefficient combination method. In addition, a feature preprocessing means are added. The experiment proves that the combination of mixed selecting combination and Pearson correlation coefficient can be stable with the performance of steganalysis before dimension reduction, but the performance dimension ratio is higher.","authors":[{"id":"a5112559828","name":"Ling Gan","orcid":"0009-0007-0263-7602","institution_ids":["i10535382"]},{"id":"a5100406419","name":"Ning Sun","orcid":"0000-0003-3844-2632","institution_ids":["i10535382"]}],"institution_ids":["i10535382"],"venue":{"id":"venue-996e30ca7ae6e1","name":"IOP Conference Series Materials Science and Engineering","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1088/1757-899x/677/2/022097","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2994909195","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1757-899x/677/2/022097","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2994909195","url":"https://openalex.org/W2994909195","query":"steganalysis spatial rich models","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1088/1757-899x/677/2/022097","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1757-899x/677/2/022097","query":"rich model image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:06:06Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-f413371c86ea92bb","title":"Boundary-based Image Forgery Detection by Fast Shallow CNN","title_zh":"","year":2018,"publication_date":"2018-08-01","abstract":"Image forgery detection is the task of detecting and localizing forged parts in tampered images. Previous works mostly focus on high resolution images using traces of resampling features, demosaicing features or sharpness of edges. However, a good detection method should also be applicable to low resolution images because compressed or resized images are common these days. To this end, we propose a Shallow Convolutional Neural Network (SCNN) capable of distinguishing the boundaries of forged regions from original edges in low resolution images. SCNN is designed to utilize the information of chroma and saturation. Based on SCNN, two approaches that are named Sliding Windows Detection (SWD) and Fast SCNN respectively, are developed to detect and localize image forgery region. Our model is evaluated on the CASIA 2.0 dataset. The results show that Fast SCNN performs well on low resolution images and achieves significant improvements over the state-of-the-art.","authors":[{"id":"a5101629880","name":"Zhongping Zhang","orcid":"0000-0002-1363-8551","institution_ids":["i5388228"]},{"id":"a5100396613","name":"Yixuan Zhang","orcid":"0000-0002-1924-9848","institution_ids":["i5388228"]},{"id":"a5108670530","name":"Zheng Zhou","orcid":"0000-0002-5976-7172","institution_ids":["i5388228"]},{"id":"a5055469774","name":"Jiebo Luo","orcid":"0000-0002-4516-9729","institution_ids":["i5388228"]}],"institution_ids":["i5388228"],"venue":null,"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/icpr.2018.8545074","arxiv_id":"1801.06732","openalex_id":"W2964341051","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icpr.2018.8545074","citation_count":47,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2964341051","url":"https://openalex.org/W2964341051","query":"image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2785157992","url":"https://openalex.org/W2785157992","query":"image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/icpr.2018.8545074","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icpr.2018.8545074","query":"image forgery localization Pattern Recognition","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:08:39Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-b9c0bae9ae5d6cbb","title":"Copy-Move Image Forgery Detection Using Redundant Keypoint Elimination Method","title_zh":"","year":2018,"publication_date":"2018-12-07","abstract":"The development of image processing and image editing software such as Adobe Photoshop®, and Photo Editor has caused created image forgery, and these images ultimately cause limitations in the information security system. This chapter presents a method that has a high accuracy in detecting forged areas, while reviewing the methods of copy-move forgery detection. Many methods are used for forgery detection in digital images, which, in general, can be divided into two active and passive methods. The format-based methods are another type of forgery detection method. The main task of these techniques is based on the Joint Photographic Experts Group image format. Digital images may be obtained from various imaging devices such as various cameras, scanners, and computer graphics imaging technology. Matching is the process of determining the correspondence between two or more features in images. The matching techniques for block-based methods can be divided into three categories: sorting, correlation, and Euclidean distance.","authors":[{"id":"a5050894875","name":"Zahra Hossein‐Nejad","orcid":"0000-0001-8309-0117","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5068728294","name":"Mehdi Nasri","orcid":"0000-0002-9254-3584","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":null,"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1201/9780429435461-26","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2950397698","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429435461-26","citation_count":7,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2950397698","url":"https://openalex.org/W2950397698","query":"copy move image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1201/9780429435461-26","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429435461-26","query":"copy move image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:29:47Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-236366dd217a11bb","title":"Image Fragile Watermarking With Two Authentication Components for Tamper Detection and Recovery","title_zh":"","year":2018,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-81189dce588e6d","name":"Lusia Rakhmawati","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-911e65498c367d","name":"Wirawan","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-3a7a9d5de42774","name":"Suwadi","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-b21ec5d0ba232c","name":"2018 International Conference on Intelligent Autonomous Systems (ICoIAS)","short